F302                             ; ---- reached from a handler ------------------------------------------------
F302                             ; chkst: stop with O unless X is in the program's own space: from the letter
F302                             ; page up to HEAPLIM, so the interpreter's stacks and whatever lies above the
F302                             ; limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but below the limit is the
F302                             ; program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there. Keeps every register.
F302   8C 82 00     CHKST:    CMPX   #LET   
