F315                             ; their handlers, at ejmp.)
F315                             ; =============================================================================
F315                             ;  Checked build: the error report. A = the letter, AT = the place; U is
F315                             ;  as the program left it, and SSAV holds S as the failing character began
F315                             ;  (see "the error entries" after `upper`).
F315                             ;  It sits here, ahead of h_num, pdec and putc, so that it reaches them with
F315                             ;  short calls. Prints
F315                             ; 
F315                             ;     CR LF
F315                             ;     Err X @ line,col CR LF
F315                             ;     <up to 16 raw characters from the place, ending early at CR, LF, NUL>
F315                             ;     CR LF
F315                             ;     Stk n:[ ...][ v]*  CR LF     (the top 8 cells, bottom to top, signed)
F315                             ;     Rtn n CR LF
F315                             ; 
F315                             ;  and goes to EXIT. Line and column count from 1: the line is one more
F315                             ;  than the LFs between PROG and the place, the column the distance from the
F315                             ;  last LF (or from PROG-1). A place below PROG is in the -n? line buffer:
F315                             ;  line 0, column = its offset there + 1. Numbers other than the cells are
F315                             ;  printed unsigned (pdec), the cells signed (h_num).
F315                             ; 
F315                             ;  The data stack may be one cell past its limit (S, U = 80FEh): the
F315                             ;  report's own cells then reach 8 bytes further down, to 80F6h, into the
F315                             ;  return stack page, so the report runs on a fresh return stack at RSREP
F315                             ;  (80F0h), below those bytes.
F315                             ; =============================================================================
F315   10 CE 80 F0  ERROR:    LDS   #RSREP   
F319   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ; the letter (pmsg and CONOUT keep B)
F31B   8D 34                  BSR   pmsg   
F31D   0D 0A 45 72 72 A0      FCB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
F323   1F 98                  TFR   B,A   
F325   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F328   8D 27                  BSR   pmsg   
F32A   20 40 A0               FCB   " @"," "+80h   
F32D                             ; the place: Y counts the lines, X walks, the cell at ,U holds the
F32D                             ; address of the last LF (PROG-1 to begin with)
F32D   10 8E 00 00            LDY   #0   
F331   8E 82 7F               LDX   #LINEBUF-1   
F334   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F336   8E 82 FF               LDX   #PROG-1   
F339   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F33B   24 23                  BHS   lc3   ; the place is below PROG: line 0
F33D   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F33F   31 21        LC1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; a line
F341   30 01        LC2:      LEAX   1,X   
F343   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F345   24 19                  BHS   lc3   
F347   A6 84                  LDA   ,X   
F349   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F34B   26 F4                  BNE   lc2   
F34D   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F34F   20 EE                  BRA   lc1   
